# Phase 2 — rel multiplicity constraints (CREATE REL TABLE ... <src>_<dst>).
# The second token bounds each source's outgoing edges, the first bounds each
# destination's incoming edges; a violation reports the offending node's offset
# with Kùzu's "fwd"/"bwd" direction wording.
-DATASET CSV empty

--

-CASE RelMultiplicityOneOne
-STATEMENT CREATE NODE TABLE N(id INT64, PRIMARY KEY(id))
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE REL TABLE R(FROM N TO N, ONE_ONE)
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE (:N {id: 1})
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE (:N {id: 2})
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE (:N {id: 3})
---- ok
-STATEMENT MATCH (a:N {id: 1}), (b:N {id: 2}) CREATE (a)-[:R]->(b)
---- ok
-STATEMENT MATCH (a:N {id: 1}), (b:N {id: 3}) CREATE (a)-[:R]->(b)
---- error
Runtime exception: Node(nodeOffset: 0) has more than one neighbour in table R in the fwd direction, which violates the rel multiplicity constraint.
-STATEMENT MATCH (a:N {id: 3}), (b:N {id: 2}) CREATE (a)-[:R]->(b)
---- error
Runtime exception: Node(nodeOffset: 1) has more than one neighbour in table R in the bwd direction, which violates the rel multiplicity constraint.

# MANY_ONE bounds the SOURCE: each src has <=1 outgoing, a dst may have many in.
-CASE RelMultiplicityManyOne
-STATEMENT CREATE NODE TABLE N(id INT64, PRIMARY KEY(id))
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE REL TABLE R(FROM N TO N, MANY_ONE)
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE (:N {id: 1})
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE (:N {id: 2})
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE (:N {id: 3})
---- ok
-STATEMENT MATCH (a:N {id: 1}), (b:N {id: 3}) CREATE (a)-[:R]->(b)
---- ok
-STATEMENT MATCH (a:N {id: 2}), (b:N {id: 3}) CREATE (a)-[:R]->(b)
---- ok
-STATEMENT MATCH (a:N {id: 1}), (b:N {id: 2}) CREATE (a)-[:R]->(b)
---- error
Runtime exception: Node(nodeOffset: 0) has more than one neighbour in table R in the fwd direction, which violates the rel multiplicity constraint.

# ONE_MANY bounds the DESTINATION: each dst has <=1 incoming, a src may have many out.
-CASE RelMultiplicityOneMany
-STATEMENT CREATE NODE TABLE N(id INT64, PRIMARY KEY(id))
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE REL TABLE R(FROM N TO N, ONE_MANY)
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE (:N {id: 1})
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE (:N {id: 2})
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE (:N {id: 3})
---- ok
-STATEMENT MATCH (a:N {id: 1}), (b:N {id: 2}) CREATE (a)-[:R]->(b)
---- ok
-STATEMENT MATCH (a:N {id: 1}), (b:N {id: 3}) CREATE (a)-[:R]->(b)
---- ok
-STATEMENT MATCH (a:N {id: 3}), (b:N {id: 2}) CREATE (a)-[:R]->(b)
---- error
Runtime exception: Node(nodeOffset: 1) has more than one neighbour in table R in the bwd direction, which violates the rel multiplicity constraint.

# MANY_MANY (the default) is unconstrained.
-CASE RelMultiplicityManyManyUnconstrained
-STATEMENT CREATE NODE TABLE N(id INT64, PRIMARY KEY(id))
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE REL TABLE R(FROM N TO N, MANY_MANY)
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE (:N {id: 1})
---- ok
-STATEMENT CREATE (:N {id: 2})
---- ok
-STATEMENT MATCH (a:N {id: 1}), (b:N {id: 2}) CREATE (a)-[:R]->(b)
---- ok
-STATEMENT MATCH (a:N {id: 1}), (b:N {id: 2}) CREATE (a)-[:R]->(b)
---- ok
-STATEMENT MATCH (a:N)-[:R]->(b:N) RETURN COUNT(*)
---- 1
2
